ins that Okafor's line-ending commit is misleading, but it lists Okafor in time.go as a blame result. It treats Kofi's activity as unknown rather than active. It does not mention Noor.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C lists Paul Borman with 6 commits for time.go and no share. It names Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer. It does not say Borman is the main author with 73%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C does not give MikeWang a share and does not credit Mei Chen with Time7. It lists Mei Chen only as a recent maintainer.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C follows the rename and lists the original authors, but says Ravi Menon is the only author in git log. It gives no Overfelt share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives no repo-wide share of departed ownership. It treats Alexander Rowe as probably one person but unconfirmed. It does not name the three active people correctly, since it lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer of time.go. It flags Kofi's 1970 date as a bad date but does not treat him as active.\", \"pass\": false}], \"D\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer D gives Paul Borman 73.0% of time.go (70.9% of non-blank lines), calls him long gone and credits Sam Okafor with none. It gives his last commit as 2016 (path/anywhere), not 2023, but the share and the departure are right.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer D gives MikeWang 81.2% of version7.go. It credits Mei Chen with Time7 at 9.4%, committed by Ravi Menon, and gives Ravi only 1.9%.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer D covers database_sql.go and names Overfelt at 39.6% of the file (within 36-52%), with Stone, Wheeler, Souza and Borman, all inactive. It does not discuss the rename explicitly, but it covers the right files.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer D says 4 of 52 people committed in the past year and hold 4.3% of the lines, so 95.7% of lines are held by departed people, which is within range. It says none of the SQL authors are active. However, it names Mei Chen as active and lists Rowe's time.go share as inactive at that path, and it does not name the three active people (Ravi, Alex, Kofi). It also recommends Mei Chen as a reviewer, who counts as departed per the ground truth.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer D says Okafor holds none of the time.go lines and notes that no bots or generated files were left out. It does not discuss Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah.\", \"pass\": false}], \"E\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer E contains only a note about a background notification and no substantive answer.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer E has no content on version7.go.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer E has no content on the SQL code.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer E has no content on who is active.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer E has no content on noise.\", \"pass\": false}], \"F\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer F credits time.go to Sam Okafor at 100%, which is the failure case.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer F gives MikeWang about 86% and Mei Chen 11 lines, which are close, and Ravi Menon 2 lines. It does not credit Ravi with Mei's lines. It lists Mei Chen's last commit as 2025-08, but it does not say Ravi committed Mei's patch, which is a minor omission. Mei's 11 lines is about 9%, consistent with the criterion.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer F follows the rename to database_sql.go and gives Overfelt 26 lines, Stone 11, Wheeler 8, Souza 8, Borman 5. The 26 lines are 44% of the 59-line file, though it states no percentage. It says all are inactive and Ravi only did the rename.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer F gives no repo-wide percentage for departed